    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-100997",
      "knowledge_point_id": "667a2ec8-c35c-52a8-a072-1d00fd8af78c",
      "knowledge_point": "Calculating Sums and Scalar Multiplication of More Than Two Vectors",
      "problem": "Let $d=9i+7j+4k,$ $e=-i+2k$ and $f=i+7j-9k.$ Find $d-(3e+f).$",
      "worked_solution": "To compute $d-(3e+f),$ we just need to perform the required operations with each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d-(3e+f) & =9i+7j+4k-(3(-i+2k)+(i+7j-9k)) \\\\  & =9i+7j+4k-((-3i+6k)+(i+7j-9k)) \\\\  & =9i+7j+4k-(-2i+7j-3k) \\\\  & =11i+7k\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
