  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930176",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-113217",
      "knowledge_point_id": "63080bb8-7a6a-505d-813a-e6c99d337064",
      "knowledge_point": "Adding and Subtracting a Number and a Rational Expression",
      "problem": "Write $3+\\frac{5-p}{p}$ as a single fraction.",
      "worked_solution": "Using the fact that $3=\\frac{3}{1},$ we can write the expression as\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{1}+\\frac{5-p}{p}.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn order to add the two fractions, we need them to have a common denominator. So, we put both fractions over a common denominator of $p$ by multiplying the top and bottom of the first fraction by $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{1}+\\frac{5-p}{p} & = \\\\ \\frac{p}{p}\\cdot \\frac{3}{1}+\\frac{5-p}{p} & = \\\\ \\frac{3p}{p}+\\frac{5-p}{p}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we add the fractions and simplify the result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3p}{p}+\\frac{5-p}{p} & = \\\\ \\frac{3p+5-p}{p} & = \\\\ \\frac{2p+5}{p}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{2p-5}{p}",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{2p+5}{p}",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{p+5}{p}",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{p-5}{p}",
              "option": "3",
              "source_option": "d"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{2(p+5)}{p}",
              "option": "4",
              "source_option": "e"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "knowledge_point_source_id": 5127,
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "provenance": {
        "activity_question": "question-113217",
        "kp_title": "Adding and Subtracting a Number and a Rational Expression",
        "kp_href": "/topics/3739#5127"
      },
      "topic_id": 3739,
